  "structure": {
    "block_count": 27,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "18 Chinese Baby Boy Names With Poetic Meaning",
        "text_sha256": "43a8a7891061c58b4d41e41dfeb7d7e23dca2bd7678e833bc24d540233b3a3b4",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Minor copy updates.",
        "text_sha256": "9820cc18b05e7b8e638e8abd1d36fb8ed59f0a5b4533b4abfc5cfe76bee4db18",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "chinese baby boy names",
        "text_sha256": "d92b18e4db6abaae15933ab14e9aa2c869f5c79034f2136418e021bb2c38e822",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Looking for a Chinese baby boy name that’s zippy — or zen? Take your pick from these poetic names, many of which evoke stunning nature scenes.",
        "text_sha256": "7a4c22d245df4e75fb0d98ef8b37914e83ba3c5bb3594831eb069b9c3636dd82",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "While many baby names in the West have long-established familial traditions, Chinese names typically get much more creative. Most Chinese names are a poetic amalgam of words that evoke beautiful imagery or aspirational character traits, referencing symbols of strength and masculinity or evoking powerful scenes inspired by nature.",
        "text_sha256": "071e3da7637a8eb01e16d51b96074045a7ab25e9b766e7f6af3d13274365c26d",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Whether you’re looking for a more sage, zen name or are a fan of the bright and bold, here are Chinese boy’s names for inspiration. (And if you're not sure whether you're having a boy or a girl, check out our favorite Chinese baby girl names , too.)",
        "text_sha256": "79605fc609aab2270d0347543ff47675254ce7b408082982773a8c65d805c562",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "1. Fenhua. A unisex name, Fenhua means “youthful and energetic.”",
        "text_sha256": "ccd6fca4b939ba29e9af5c7b30bec27b3c78635bd8a8831de5108aec93b30281",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "2. Haoyu. Parents with a passion for the cosmos might consider this strong baby boy name, which means “vast universe.”",
        "text_sha256": "deb0d7a26cd82c5293d75bd305d74e7e474ef92e200c913770a1b893ddb0e7d4",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "3. Haitao. Have a strong love of the sea — and hoping your little one will, too? Try the name Haitao, which means “a strong and powerful ocean wave.”",
        "text_sha256": "117e991930ff23db9fe8312d4dcee821591e6581eaca4ede9b05defc5594265c",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "4. Junfeng. There’s nothing more satisfying than finishing a steep hike to behold the breath-taking views. That’s the picture that this name paints — a majestic mountain scape seen from the ideal vantage point.",
        "text_sha256": "68a600343969a99b9dee5ffa203cf4c0316733d8cc394f3f8cff35e66120401f",
        "word_count": 34
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "5. Lixin. A great name for a bright and sunny boy, Lixin (pronounced lee-shin) means “a glorious and beautiful sunrise.”",
        "text_sha256": "e65c97823bcc883e8bdde205aac8fe459a7cd9e5c88433f78a2a8aff9b64cb82",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "6. Lingyun. \"Ling\" means “lofty,” or “high up,” while \"yun\" means “cloud.” Choose this imaginative name for a boy who’s sure to have exceptional aspirations.",
        "text_sha256": "e0b62adbc20730b23d63b554dd5ffc79fa869d4504428f28c5dfbbb5be81b070",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "7. Qianfan. A name that brings to mind nautical imagery, Qianfan (chee-an fan) means “a thousand sails.”",
        "text_sha256": "251d2c3f28da56be6642655009f329adcd227d6a6ad0c244807d6ef9e86eed69",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "8. Shuchang. Shuchang is a great name if you’d like a gentleman with a happy demeanour. The name means “easy-going and blissful.”",
        "text_sha256": "8a5bdc11de3eb667da92053d30758e95319bd904ec7d0762c7d6ac337ec5876f",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "9. Sile. Pronounced si-le, this name is for boys who are cheerful, optimistic, and always happy. What more could you want for your little one!",
        "text_sha256": "648f205e5b7bcb509f25e262102a1388410783fd7945af24d2911ea03a48b7b5",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "10. Sicong. Convinced your baby guy will be the next Bach or Einstein? Try out the name Sicong (pronounced si-ts-o-ng), which means “clever and original.”",
        "text_sha256": "0af0a72322b486834df40b84161141d8cc4b307b497b96812df9435296a03781",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "11. Tianyu. You can’t go wrong with this very classic Chinese name, which means “heavenly jade.”",
        "text_sha256": "86cb11a9d4bb7ba42294fa2c8983cf7fe5239fdbd2a2135519ad35349822b5cd",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "12. Xiyang. If Lixin doesn’t quite do it for you, maybe try Xiyang (shee yan-g), meaning “the evening sun” or “sunset.”",
        "text_sha256": "2142ba8db67792e96dc381aa036ac00ecd761b3562021fe7746c651e3576e29d",
        "word_count": 21
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "13. Xuesong. Another name for nature lovers, \"xue\" (pronounced shoo-ye) means “snow,” while song means “pine tree.” Together the name evokes pine trees covered in a fresh blanket of snow: A picturesque name for a winter baby.",
        "text_sha256": "c25310b308e3a1f06dca0ff9fae0cc0716ab8bf083ffe28834a391d01058bbd7",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "14. Yangfang. Perfect for a family with nautical proclivities, this name elicits the image of grand and majestic sails catching wind. A great name for your bold and adventurous little boy!",
        "text_sha256": "79a1ffd0f70e9b01d6397af16b375d0a29833c0a57ac9c741c9659f5843dffed",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "15. Yufei. A tranquil yet strong name, Yufei (pronounced yu-fay) means “feather in flight.”",
        "text_sha256": "9ee2416c58e49b959750493271522dc1ef7434c12ff52b376b19d052e0c39467",
        "word_count": 14
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "16. Yulong. Meaning “jade dragon,” this classic Chinese name is a beautiful pick for your little guy.",
        "text_sha256": "41511a0f9b9b43e85e76f10007c7dcda310f23b0f1d5f4a3a1f6037bbf5fff38",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "17. Yuze. Pronounced yu-ze, this evocative name means “a refreshing monsoon after a humid day.”",
        "text_sha256": "ab6373005bd8c4d40c1675844fa8348deb388bbb1043c568553ccf60ce4d364a",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "18. Zhiyuan. Pronounced jir-yu-wan, this name sets the path for your ambitious boy. It means “visionary” or a “go-getting dreamer.”",
        "text_sha256": "589f8e7c4a3f0a10bed91bf4bf2f2940d02469c354e868577e507d5f8897afa2",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Pronounced jir-yu-wan, this name sets the path for your ambitious boy. It means “visionary” or a “go-getting dreamer.”",
        "text_sha256": "facfe4096b0e8c73765b460b4ba3e098f96ef41c311fc1fbd66636cd8c901a24",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Still hunting for the perfect baby name? Open the What to Expect app for the top 1,000 names (and plenty of unique ones, too) — plus get week-by-week updates on the tiny human you’re naming.",
        "text_sha256": "70bf66f4138b23f0ee54f40a3562886af0f6d501fab7189be8c0284cdd133cb5",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Marina Wang is a freelance journalist living in Calgary, Canada. On her off days, she will gladly eschew all responsibilities to sing songs and dance with her baby niece. Wang has a special interest in science and travel and has written for publications such as Science Magazine , Atlas Obscura , Mental Floss , Canadian Geographic and the CBC. She is second-generation Chinese and a native Mandarin speaker. She holds a Bachelor of Science degree in zoology and a Master's in journalism from Carleton University.",
        "text_sha256": "ff0ed08fe8d0c03d460e7f68321431c3a3bfc3f4b85eed35d29c0b842a5850e6",
        "word_count": 85
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 673,
    "heading_count": 1
  },
